== bedrock deploy (hidden false)
Deploy the app in a source directory: build, start, check, switch the edge, retire the old revision.

Usage:
  bedrock deploy <source-dir> [flags]

Flags:
      --digest string                apply only if the plan is still the one with this digest; implies --yes
      --manifest string              the manifest at the source's root, for a source that holds several apps (default "bedrock.yaml")
      --plan                         show the plan and change nothing
      --restore-postgres string      a pg_dump file to load into the app's empty database first
      --restore-volume stringArray   name=file.tar.gz to unpack into an empty volume first
      --to string                    send the source to a machine over SSH, such as bedrock@203.0.113.7, and deploy it there ($BEDROCK_SSH replaces ssh)
      --yes                          apply without asking

Global Flags:
      --json               print JSON, one object per line
      --socket string      the daemon's socket; the local kernel is used when nothing answers (default "/run/bedrock/bedrock.sock")
      --state-dir string   where bedrock keeps its state (default "~/.bedrock")
