== bedrock git (hidden false)
Deploy by pushing: which keys may push which apps, remotes, and GitHub webhooks.

Usage:
  bedrock git [command]

Available Commands:
  allow       Let an SSH key deploy an app with git push or bedrock deploy --to. The key comes from the argument or stdin.
  branch      Choose the branch whose pushes deploy an app (main by default).
  deny        Stop a key from deploying an app; a key left with no apps is removed.
  keys        List the keys that may push, and the apps each deploys.
  remote      Print the git remote that deploys an app.
  webhook     Deploy an app when GitHub says its branch moved; prints what to paste into GitHub, once.
  webhooks    List the webhooks and what their last delivery did.

Global Flags:
      --json               print JSON, one object per line
      --socket string      the daemon's socket; the local kernel is used when nothing answers (default "/run/bedrock/bedrock.sock")
      --state-dir string   where bedrock keeps its state (default "~/.bedrock")

