== bedrock run (hidden false)
Run a one-off command with a workload's image, environment, secrets and volumes.
Run a one-off command with a workload's image, environment, secrets and volumes.

--secret gives the command more of the app's secrets by name; their values
never leave the machine. --stdin hands this command's standard input to
the command, for a value that must appear in no argument, log or record:
the command then runs here, not in the daemon, and exits with the
command's own exit code.
Usage:
  bedrock run <app> [workload] -- <command...> [flags]

Flags:
      --plan                 show what would run and change nothing
      --secret stringArray   give the command this secret of the app too (repeatable)
      --stdin                pass standard input to the command; it runs in this process

Global Flags:
      --json               print JSON, one object per line
      --socket string      the daemon's socket; the local kernel is used when nothing answers (default "/run/bedrock/bedrock.sock")
      --state-dir string   where bedrock keeps its state (default "~/.bedrock")
== bedrock secret (hidden false)
Keep an app's secrets sealed on this machine.

Usage:
  bedrock secret [command]

Available Commands:
  copy        Give another app the same value of a secret, without showing it.
  export      Seal one secret for another machine; prints only age ciphertext.
  import      Read a secret sealed for this machine from stdin, without showing it.
  list        List the names in the current version. Values are never shown.
  recipient   Print the machine's public encryption recipient, creating its key if needed.
  remove      Drop a name from the next version.
  set         Store a value, read from stdin or typed without echo. Never pass it as an argument.
  versions    List every version and the names it holds.

Global Flags:
      --json               print JSON, one object per line
      --socket string      the daemon's socket; the local kernel is used when nothing answers (default "/run/bedrock/bedrock.sock")
      --state-dir string   where bedrock keeps its state (default "~/.bedrock")

Use "bedrock secret [command] --help" for more information about a command.
== bedrock secret copy (hidden false)
Give another app the same value of a secret, without showing it.
Give another app the same value of a secret, without showing it: for
two apps that must share a credential, such as a worker that pairs with
the product that made its token. The value never leaves the machine's
store. Copying the same value again changes nothing.
Usage:
  bedrock secret copy <from-app> <NAME> <to-app> [flags]

Global Flags:
      --json               print JSON, one object per line
      --socket string      the daemon's socket; the local kernel is used when nothing answers (default "/run/bedrock/bedrock.sock")
      --state-dir string   where bedrock keeps its state (default "~/.bedrock")
